# 1.1) Bronze: Ingest Source Data

On this page, you'll create the pipeline and define Bronze tables that ingest the 3 source {{ 'tables' if mode != 'files' else 'datasets' }} ({{ s.sources | map(attribute='name') | map('code') | join(', ') }}) as-is.

## Task 1 - Create the pipeline { #task-1 }

1. Click **New** in the top left of the sidebar, then click **ETL pipeline**.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-1-01-new-etl-pipeline.png', 'New > ETL pipeline') }}

2. The Lakeflow Pipelines Editor opens. Click the pipeline name at the top of the screen and enter `<your_name>_{{ s.naming.pipeline }}`. For example, if your name is {{ s.naming.example_user | capitalize }}, enter `{{ s.naming.example_user }}_{{ s.naming.pipeline }}`.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-1-02-pipeline-name.png', 'Pipeline name input') }}

3. Click the default catalog and schema next to the pipeline name. Select the catalog `{{ cat }}` (e.g., `{{ ex_cat }}`) and schema `default`, then click **Save**. All tables created by the pipeline will be stored in this location.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-1-03-default-catalog-schema.png', 'Select default catalog and schema') }}

4. Select **SQL** as the source code language. When the **Changing default language** dialog appears, click **Confirm**.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-1-04-language-sql.png', 'Select SQL language') }}

!!! info "Compute settings"
    The pipeline uses **Serverless compute** and **Unity Catalog** by default. For this lab, use the default settings as-is.

