## Understanding the code

| Syntax | Description |
|---|---|
{% if mode == 'files' %}
| `CREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE` | Defines a Streaming Table. Each time the pipeline runs, only newly arrived files are processed incrementally. |
| `FROM STREAM read_files('{{ s.sources[0].path }}', ...)` | Reads files from cloud storage with Auto Loader. New files are discovered automatically on each run. |
| `_ingested_at`, `_source` | Audit columns that record when data was ingested and which file it came from (`_metadata.file_path`). |
{% elif mode == 'federation' %}
| `CREATE OR REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW` | Defines a Materialized View. Federated sources are read in batch, so Bronze snapshots the source on each run. |
| `FROM {{ s.sources[0].ref }}` | Reads the {{ s.architecture.federation.system }} table in place through the foreign catalog. No copy job is needed. |
| `_ingested_at`, `_source` | Audit columns that record when and where data was ingested. |
{% else %}
| `CREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE` | Defines a Streaming Table. Each time the pipeline runs, only newly arrived data is processed incrementally. |
| `FROM STREAM({{ s.sources[0].ref }})` | Reads the source table as a streaming source. |
| `_ingested_at`, `_source` | Audit columns that record when and where data was ingested. |
{% endif %}
| `TBLPROPERTIES ('quality' = 'bronze')` | Identifies which layer the table belongs to. |

!!! tip "Role of the Bronze layer"
    The Bronze layer preserves source data **unchanged**. If cleansing logic changes later, you can reprocess from Bronze without re-ingesting the raw data.

!!! success "Congratulations!"
    You've created the pipeline and defined 3 Bronze tables. On the next page, you'll define the Silver and Gold tables.
